 build:build('Count each event stream before combining it','Joining raw visits to raw readings would multiply the event rows for an asset.','Count visits by asset into visits and readings by asset into readings. Inner-join those two summaries for assets present in both, carrying readings with an empty prefix. Report asset_id, visits and readings in asset order.',{visits:'Inspection event records',readings:'Reading event records'},[sample('Summaries avoid the raw-event multiplication',{visits:inspections,readings},[{asset_id:'P1',visits:3,readings:2},{asset_id:'P2',visits:2,readings:1},{asset_id:'P3',visits:1,readings:1}]),sample('More readings do not create more visits',{visits:[{asset_id:'P1',inspection_id:1},{asset_id:'P1',inspection_id:2}],readings:[{asset_id:'P1',reading_id:1},{asset_id:'P1',reading_id:2},{asset_id:'P1',reading_id:3}]},[{asset_id:'P1',visits:2,readings:3}])],sort(joinRows(group(s('visits'),'asset_id','count rows','inspection_id','visits'),group(s('readings'),'asset_id','count rows','reading_id','readings'),'inner','readings',''),'asset_id ASC'),'Each branch establishes one row per asset before the match. The SQL challenge extends this construction to retain the entire asset register.',['Group both streams before connecting them. Counting after a raw join counts pairs.']),
